WEBVTT
TITLE Disjoint-set forests (union-find): parent pointers, union by rank, path compression and the inverse Ackermann bound — GATE Visual Explainer
NOTE Timings are estimated from the lesson timeline (speaking-rate based), not measured from recorded audio.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.500
Six elements, each alone in its own set. A union merges two sets. A find asks which set an element is in.

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:15.000
The usual representation is a forest: one parent pointer per element, and the root of each tree names the set.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Find follows parent pointers to a root. Union points one root at the other. The cost of both is the number of hops.

4
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:30.000
Two correct implementations can produce different trees, so the tree shape is the whole subject.

5
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.500
Link every new element under the previous one and the eight elements form a chain of height seven.

6
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Find of zero now walks seven edges. At n elements that same call walks n minus one, so a single find is Theta of n.

7
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.500
Repeat that find m times with no repair and the total is Theta of m times n: the sequence is quadratic for no reason.

8
00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:00.000
Two independent repairs exist: change which root goes under which, and change what find leaves behind.

9
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Union by rank: keep a rank per node, start it at zero, and attach the lower-ranked root under the higher.

10
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:15.000
A root of rank k holds at least two to the k nodes, so no rank exceeds log base two of n. Measured: no violation up to 64.

11
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:22.500
Eight elements, seven unions: the parent array is 0 0 0 2 0 4 4 6, the root holds all eight, and the height is three.

12
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Union by size is the same rule counted differently: it stores a node count, not a rank. Different array, same logarithmic bound.

13
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.500
Find of zero on the chain walks seven edges and returns the root. Path compression then makes every node on that path point at the root.

14
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:45.000
The same find again costs one hop. Measured on eight elements: seven hops, then one, then one.

15
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Compression never changes a rank, so after find of seven the root still has rank three while the real height has fallen to two.

16
00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:00.000
Three rewiring variants: two-pass compression, path halving, path splitting. Different pointers, same purpose.

17
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.500
No repair: a find is Theta of n in the worst case, because the chain is always available as an input sequence.

18
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Union by rank alone: every find is O of log n, and the bound is tight, because a balanced merge sequence attains log base two of n.

19
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:22.500
Compression alone: one find can still cost n, but any sequence of m operations costs O of m log n. Tarjan and van Leeuwen, 1984.

20
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:30.000
Both together: O of m alpha of n for the whole sequence. Measured here at 1.93 hops per operation against 60.93 with no repair.

21
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Ackermann of k and j: A of zero and j is j plus one; A of k and zero is A of k minus one and one; otherwise it is A of k minus one applied to A of k and j minus one.

22
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:45.000
A of k and one gives 2, 3, 5, 13, 65533. So alpha is 1 up to 3, 2 up to 5, 3 up to 13, 4 up to 65533, and 5 after that.

23
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:52.500
So alpha of n is not one, and it is not a constant: it grows without bound, just astronomically slowly.

24
00:02:52.500 --> 00:03:00.000
And the bound is on a sequence: one operation in that sequence may still walk a long path. Amortised is not per operation.

25
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:07.500
Kruskal sorts the edges and asks one question per edge: are these two endpoints already connected? Two finds answer it.

26
00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:15.000
Six vertices, nine edges: five accepted with total weight 14, four rejected. Eighteen finds and five unions, twelve hops.

27
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:22.500
The counts are fixed by the graph, not by the weights: two finds per edge, n minus one unions, and m minus n plus one rejects.

28
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:30.000
With the sorting removed the cost is the union-find cost: O of m alpha of n with both repairs, O of m log n with rank alone.

29
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:37.500
Ten elements, eight union calls, seven successful: three sets remain, which is n minus the successful unions.

30
00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:45.000
The same number is read the other way: count the roots, the elements that are their own parent. Three here.

31
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:52.500
After n minus one successful unions on n elements, one set remains: the graph is connected, and the forest is a single tree.

32
00:03:52.500 --> 00:04:00.000
A union that returns false is information, not an error: the two elements are already connected, and in Kruskal that is a cycle.

33
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:07.500
A disjoint-set forest only merges. There is no split, no delete, and no way to undo a union.

34
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:15.000
It answers same or different, not how. The parent pointers are not a path in the graph.

35
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:22.500
It detects cycles in undirected graphs only. Two vertices joined in both directions are a directed cycle and not an undirected one.

36
00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:30.000
It cannot list the members of a set either. That needs a second structure, such as a member list per root.

37
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:37.500
First: which linking rule? Without one, the parent array is not determined, and a question that asks for it must have said.

38
00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:45.000
Second: is compression on? It makes the array depend on the order of the finds, not only on the unions.

39
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:52.500
Third: count hops, not operations, and state n and m. A bound without its two parameters is not a bound.

40
00:04:52.500 --> 00:05:00.000
Three sentences to write: no repair Theta of n; rank alone O of log n and tight; both together O of m alpha of n amortised.

